      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(channels): honor configured read target policies",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nChannel message actions did not consistently apply the active account and conversation target\npolicies before provider reads or mutations. The affected paths included message, reaction, pin,\nmember, search, and information actions across bundled channel plugins.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis moves target authorization into each channel owner's action boundary and carries trusted\ncurrent-conversation context through Gateway, agent, plugin, Codex, and Copilot tool paths.\nProvider content is fetched only after the action has resolved and accepted its target.\n\nThe implementation also aligns adjacent provider contracts:\n\n- Feishu authorizes message-id reaction paths before provider content reads and preserves\n  reaction ownership during clear-all.\n- Microsoft Teams uses the shared guarded-fetch transport rather than incompatible custom\n  `globalThis.fetch` wrappers.\n- Google Chat advertises only its supported outbound text action and rejects outbound attachment\n  aliases before provider access while preserving inbound attachments.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCurrent-conversation actions and explicitly configured cross-conversation actions continue to\nwork. Provider-accessible targets outside the configured policy now fail closed before content\nreads or mutations. Google Chat outbound service-account behavior is text-only; inbound text,\nthreads, and attachments remain supported.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact candidate: `21eac9cb387a43c27bb842c02280e92bc4311353`\n\n- Fresh Codex autoreview: no actionable findings.\n- Full build passed.\n- Exact-tree `check:changed` passed.\n- Final focused Testbox run: 77 passed, Testbox\n  `tbx_01kwzj29xnz7dr4r1k0t3s04ax`.\n- Broader affected extension suite: 1,261 passed.\n- Live exact-head provider proof passed for Discord, Slack, Feishu/Lark, Google Chat, Matrix,\n  and Microsoft Teams.\n- Live Codex GPT-5.5 harness and logged-in GitHub Copilot tool bridge passed.\n- Live cases covered current and configured targets, blocked targets, DM and group/room/space\n  routing, threads where supported, wrong-account rejection where applicable, reactions and\n  ownership-preserving clear, pins, provider metadata, restart/resume, and inbound attachments.\n- Google Chat provider-side verification confirmed real DM, current-space, configured-space,\n  same-thread, blocked-space, and attachment flows.\n- Baseline comparison against `origin/main` at\n  `9dbb1ed3d24655a144be1fe58a652f13ebe9f311` reproduced the prior behavior on affected\n  channel paths while unchanged Copilot behavior remained green.\n",
        "branch": "fix/channel-read-policy-gates",
